# **PART III — World presentation, audio and player experience**

## **Phase 9 — Environment, MP4 arenas and visual cohesion**

Priority: High • Living world and chamber transitions

**Objective:** Make the painted environments, rendered characters, combat effects and chamber progression feel like a single cohesive game world.

### **9.1 Retain the existing MP4 arena approach**

Our plan is to preserve high-quality painted arenas and animated backgrounds.

Do not replace them with generic full-3D rooms simply to gain unrestricted camera movement.

Instead, enhance their presentation through rendering, compositing, interaction and environmental animation.

### **9.2 Audit all eight chambers**

Each chamber requires evaluation of:

- Art direction.
- Color composition.
- Background resolution.
- Animation loop quality.
- Foreground and background integration.
- Depth and perspective.
- Character scaling.
- Floor placement.
- Lighting.
- Combat visibility.
- Loading behavior.
- Transition quality.

### **9.3 Fix static-image-to-video snapping**

One of our identified problems was the visible switch from a static background to the animated MP4.

Implement a reliable preload and display strategy.

The first visible frame should correspond appropriately to the video content.

Never replace a well-composed background with an unrelated-looking video during gameplay.

### **9.4 Improve character/environment integration**

Rudra, enemies and bosses must appear grounded within the scene.

Improve contact shadows, feet positioning, foreground occlusion, depth sorting, lighting direction, color grading and environment scale.

This is especially important because the game combines 3D characters with painterly arena backgrounds.

### **9.5 Add environmental responsiveness**

Where technically practical, incorporate:

- Ground dust from impacts.
- Ambient particles.
- Heat and atmospheric effects.
- Subtle background motion.
- Localized lighting changes.
- Collision debris.
- Environmental effects appropriate to each chamber.

These elements must support the existing artwork rather than obscure it.

### **9.6 Improve portals and room transitions**

Our later discussions specifically added higher-quality portal and chamber-transition presentation.

The portal system should communicate where the player is going and when a chamber has been completed.

Improve the visual entrance and exit treatment, transition timing, environmental continuity and loading reliability.

Ensure reliable movement between the Vaitarani hub and the existing chambers, including restart and post-boss flows.

### **9.7 Hub and chamber cohesion**

Savitri's boat and the Vaitarani should remain visually distinct but consistent with the larger game's art direction.

Environmental lighting, audio atmosphere, player presentation and progression transitions should reinforce the mood.

### **9.8 Completion gate**

Every chamber looks coherent, the characters appear grounded, MP4 backgrounds transition smoothly, room progression is reliable, and environment effects enhance rather than distract from gameplay.

